    "ticket-exit-line-focus-show-course-details-add-line-to-plan-72333a75": {
      "id": "ticket-exit-line-focus-show-course-details-add-line-to-plan-72333a75",
      "goal_id": "goal_graph-line-focus-details-and-plan-from-line_705e",
      "title": "Exit line-focus, show course details, add line to plan",
      "brief": "After selecting a colored graph line, users can return to the current map, see the clicked course in the inspector, and add that line's catalog courses to a chosen semester without changing map scope.",
      "acceptance": [
        "With a relationship selected, a visible Exit line focus control, Escape from the graph layout (including the inspector), and a click on empty map all clear the selection and restore the previous map scope and zoom; they do not switch depth to This course's full chain.",
        "Clicking a course card updates the inspector heading, title, credits, and description for that course even while a line is selected; it does not require Full course details. Dimmed cards remain clickable.",
        "With a line selected, Add this line to a semester lists the line's program courses, skips externals and already-recorded codes, and addCourse-equivalent inserts the rest into the chosen term without exceeding 32 courses; npm test and npm run typecheck pass."
      ],
